  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency action for conflict displaced communities in Alto Baud&#xf3;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFODs partner SNPS/Cartias Colombiana are responding to the humanitarian emergency caused by the forced displacement and confinement of 1,200 people (267 families) due to combat between ELN guerrillas and AGC paramilitaries in Choco Department, Colombia.
The project aims to support 800 people (162 families) with food and NFI, as well as Kitchen kit, sleeping kit (including mosquito nets -this is a malaria area). The combat has destroyed their crops and they lost their animals, so there is also an agriculture and livestock component. They are also thinking of hiring staff locally to implement the project.</narrative>
  </description>
